  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-48096",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "OpenFGA: OpenFGA: Incorrect authorization due to cache key collision in iterator caching"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "OpenFGA is an authorization/permission engine built for developers. Prior to version 1.16.0, when iterator caching is enabled, two distinct check requests can produce the same cache key, leading to OpenFGA reusing an earlier cached result for a subsequent request. This issue has been patched in version 1.16.0."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-48096",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-48096\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: github.com/openfga/openfga\nFixed Version: 1.16.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-48096](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-48096)\nOpenFGA is an authorization/permission engine built for developers. Prior to version 1.16.0, when iterator caching is enabled, two distinct check requests can produce the same cache key, leading to OpenFGA reusing an earlier cached result for a subsequent request. This issue has been patched in version 1.16.0.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-48096**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|github.com/openfga/openfga|1.16.0|[CVE-2026-48096](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-48096)|\n\nOpenFGA is an authorization/permission engine built for developers. Prior to version 1.16.0, when iterator caching is enabled, two distinct check requests can produce the same cache key, leading to OpenFGA reusing an earlier cached result for a subsequent request. This issue has been patched in version 1.16.0."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-55689",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "OpenFGA: OIDC audience validation skipped when --authn-oidc-audience is unset"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "## Description\n\nOpenFGA's OIDC authenticator skipped JWT audience (`aud`) validation when no audience was configured.\nIn deployments where one identity provider issues tokens for multiple services,\na token minted for an unrelated service could authenticate to OpenFGA.\n\n## Preconditions\n\nThis applies if the following preconditions are met:\n\n1. You run OpenFGA with `authn.method` set to `oidc`.\n2. You configured `authn.oidc.issuer` but did **not** set\n   `authn.oidc.audience` (`--authn-oidc-audience` / `OPENFGA_AUTHN_OIDC_AUDIENCE`).\n\n## Fix\n\nUpgrade to OpenFGA 1.18.0 or greater. OpenFGA now refuses to start in `oidc`\nmode unless both `authn.oidc.issuer` and `authn.oidc.audience` are set, and the\n`aud` claim is always validated.\n\n## Acknowledgements\n\nOpenFGA would like to thank https://github.com/0xVijay for the report."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-55689",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-55689\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: github.com/openfga/openfga\nFixed Version: 1.18.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-55689](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-55689)\n## Description\n\nOpenFGA's OIDC authenticator skipped JWT audience (`aud`) validation when no audience was configured.\nIn deployments where one identity provider issues tokens for multiple services,\na token minted for an unrelated service could authenticate to OpenFGA.\n\n## Preconditions\n\nThis applies if the following preconditions are met:\n\n1. You run OpenFGA with `authn.method` set to `oidc`.\n2. You configured `authn.oidc.issuer` but did **not** set\n   `authn.oidc.audience` (`--authn-oidc-audience` / `OPENFGA_AUTHN_OIDC_AUDIENCE`).\n\n## Fix\n\nUpgrade to OpenFGA 1.18.0 or greater. OpenFGA now refuses to start in `oidc`\nmode unless both `authn.oidc.issuer` and `authn.oidc.audience` are set, and the\n`aud` claim is always validated.\n\n## Acknowledgements\n\nOpenFGA would like to thank https://github.com/0xVijay for the report.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-55689**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|github.com/openfga/openfga|1.18.0|[CVE-2026-55689](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-55689)|\n\n## Description\n\nOpenFGA's OIDC authenticator skipped JWT audience (`aud`) validation when no audience was configured.\nIn deployments where one identity provider issues tokens for multiple services,\na token minted for an unrelated service could authenticate to OpenFGA.\n\n## Preconditions\n\nThis applies if the following preconditions are met:\n\n1. You run OpenFGA with `authn.method` set to `oidc`.\n2. You configured `authn.oidc.issuer` but did **not** set\n   `authn.oidc.audience` (`--authn-oidc-audience` / `OPENFGA_AUTHN_OIDC_AUDIENCE`).\n\n## Fix\n\nUpgrade to OpenFGA 1.18.0 or greater. OpenFGA now refuses to start in `oidc`\nmode unless both `authn.oidc.issuer` and `authn.oidc.audience` are set, and the\n`aud` claim is always validated.\n\n## Acknowledgements\n\nOpenFGA would like to thank https://github.com/0xVijay for the report."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.8,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "6.8",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-55170",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "OpenFGA Improper Policy Enforcement"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "## Description\n\nIn OpenFGA, when MySQL is being used as the datastore, two distinct check requests can return the same response.\n\n## Preconditions\n\nThis applies if the following preconditions are met:\n\n1. You run OpenFGA with MySQL as the datastore\n2. Your authorization decisions rely on case-sensitive user strings.\n\n## Fix\nUpgrade to OpenFGA 1.18.0 or greater.\n\n## Acknowledgements\nOpenFGA would like to thank @sahajamoth for the detailed report."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-55170",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-55170\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: github.com/openfga/openfga\nFixed Version: 1.18.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-55170](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-55170)\n## Description\n\nIn OpenFGA, when MySQL is being used as the datastore, two distinct check requests can return the same response.\n\n## Preconditions\n\nThis applies if the following preconditions are met:\n\n1. You run OpenFGA with MySQL as the datastore\n2. Your authorization decisions rely on case-sensitive user strings.\n\n## Fix\nUpgrade to OpenFGA 1.18.0 or greater.\n\n## Acknowledgements\nOpenFGA would like to thank @sahajamoth for the detailed report.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-55170**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|github.com/openfga/openfga|1.18.0|[CVE-2026-55170](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-55170)|\n\n## Description\n\nIn OpenFGA, when MySQL is being used as the datastore, two distinct check requests can return the same response.\n\n## Preconditions\n\nThis applies if the following preconditions are met:\n\n1. You run OpenFGA with MySQL as the datastore\n2. Your authorization decisions rely on case-sensitive user strings.\n\n## Fix\nUpgrade to OpenFGA 1.18.0 or greater.\n\n## Acknowledgements\nOpenFGA would like to thank @sahajamoth for the detailed report."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 2.1,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:P/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-40179",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Prometheus has Stored XSS via metric names and label values in Prometheus web UI tooltips and metrics explorer"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Prometheus is an open-source monitoring system and time series database. Versions 3.0 through 3.5.1 and 3.6.0 through 3.11.1 have stored cross-site scripting vulnerabilities in multiple components of the Prometheus web UI where metric names and label values are injected into innerHTML without escaping. In both the Mantine UI and old React UI, chart tooltips on the Graph page render metric names containing HTML/JavaScript without sanitization. In the old React UI, the Metric Explorer fuzzy search results use dangerouslySetInnerHTML without escaping, and heatmap cell tooltips interpolate le label values without sanitization. With Prometheus v3.x defaulting to UTF-8 metric and label name validation, characters like \u003c, \u003e, and \" are now valid in metric names and labels. An attacker who can inject metrics via a compromised scrape target, remote write, or OTLP receiver endpoint can execute arbitrary JavaScript in the browser of any Prometheus user who views the metric in the Graph UI, potentially enabling configuration exfiltration, data deletion, or Prometheus shutdown depending on enabled flags. This issue has been fixed in versions 3.5.2 and 3.11.2. If developers are unable to immediately update, the following workarounds are recommended: ensure that the remote write receiver (--web.enable-remote-write-receiver) and the OTLP receiver (--web.enable-otlp-receiver) are not exposed to untrusted sources; verify that all scrape targets are trusted and not under attacker control; avoid enabling admin or mutating API endpoints (e.g., --web.enable-admin-api or --web.enable-lifecycle) in environments where untrusted data may be ingested; and refrain from clicking untrusted links, particularly those containing functions such as label_replace, as they may generate poisoned label names and values."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-40179",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-40179\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: github.com/prometheus/prometheus\nFixed Version: 0.311.2-0.20260410083055-07c6232d159b\nLink: [CVE-2026-40179](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-40179)\nPrometheus is an open-source monitoring system and time series database. Versions 3.0 through 3.5.1 and 3.6.0 through 3.11.1 have stored cross-site scripting vulnerabilities in multiple components of the Prometheus web UI where metric names and label values are injected into innerHTML without escaping. In both the Mantine UI and old React UI, chart tooltips on the Graph page render metric names containing HTML/JavaScript without sanitization. In the old React UI, the Metric Explorer fuzzy search results use dangerouslySetInnerHTML without escaping, and heatmap cell tooltips interpolate le label values without sanitization. With Prometheus v3.x defaulting to UTF-8 metric and label name validation, characters like \u003c, \u003e, and \" are now valid in metric names and labels. An attacker who can inject metrics via a compromised scrape target, remote write, or OTLP receiver endpoint can execute arbitrary JavaScript in the browser of any Prometheus user who views the metric in the Graph UI, potentially enabling configuration exfiltration, data deletion, or Prometheus shutdown depending on enabled flags. This issue has been fixed in versions 3.5.2 and 3.11.2. If developers are unable to immediately update, the following workarounds are recommended: ensure that the remote write receiver (--web.enable-remote-write-receiver) and the OTLP receiver (--web.enable-otlp-receiver) are not exposed to untrusted sources; verify that all scrape targets are trusted and not under attacker control; avoid enabling admin or mutating API endpoints (e.g., --web.enable-admin-api or --web.enable-lifecycle) in environments where untrusted data may be ingested; and refrain from clicking untrusted links, particularly those containing functions such as label_replace, as they may generate poisoned label names and values.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-40179**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|github.com/prometheus/prometheus|0.311.2-0.20260410083055-07c6232d159b|[CVE-2026-40179](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-40179)|\n\nPrometheus is an open-source monitoring system and time series database. Versions 3.0 through 3.5.1 and 3.6.0 through 3.11.1 have stored cross-site scripting vulnerabilities in multiple components of the Prometheus web UI where metric names and label values are injected into innerHTML without escaping. In both the Mantine UI and old React UI, chart tooltips on the Graph page render metric names containing HTML/JavaScript without sanitization. In the old React UI, the Metric Explorer fuzzy search results use dangerouslySetInnerHTML without escaping, and heatmap cell tooltips interpolate le label values without sanitization. With Prometheus v3.x defaulting to UTF-8 metric and label name validation, characters like \u003c, \u003e, and \" are now valid in metric names and labels. An attacker who can inject metrics via a compromised scrape target, remote write, or OTLP receiver endpoint can execute arbitrary JavaScript in the browser of any Prometheus user who views the metric in the Graph UI, potentially enabling configuration exfiltration, data deletion, or Prometheus shutdown depending on enabled flags. This issue has been fixed in versions 3.5.2 and 3.11.2. If developers are unable to immediately update, the following workarounds are recommended: ensure that the remote write receiver (--web.enable-remote-write-receiver) and the OTLP receiver (--web.enable-otlp-receiver) are not exposed to untrusted sources; verify that all scrape targets are trusted and not under attacker control; avoid enabling admin or mutating API endpoints (e.g., --web.enable-admin-api or --web.enable-lifecycle) in environments where untrusted data may be ingested; and refrain from clicking untrusted links, particularly those containing functions such as label_replace, as they may generate poisoned label names and values."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.1,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N",
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 5.3,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "6.1",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-44903",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Prometheus is an open-source monitoring system and time series databas ..."
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Prometheus is an open-source monitoring system and time series database. From 2.49.0 to before 3.5.3 and 3.11.3, in the Prometheus server's legacy web UI (enabled via the command-line flag --enable-feature=old-ui), the histogram heatmap chart view does not escape le label values when inserting them into the HTML for use as axis tick mark labels. An attacker who can inject crafted metrics can execute JavaScript in the browser of any Prometheus user who views the metric in the heatmap chart UI. This vulnerability is fixed in 3.5.3 and 3.11.3."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-44903",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-44903\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: github.com/prometheus/prometheus\nFixed Version: 0.311.3\nLink: [CVE-2026-44903](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-44903)\nPrometheus is an open-source monitoring system and time series database. From 2.49.0 to before 3.5.3 and 3.11.3, in the Prometheus server's legacy web UI (enabled via the command-line flag --enable-feature=old-ui), the histogram heatmap chart view does not escape le label values when inserting them into the HTML for use as axis tick mark labels. An attacker who can inject crafted metrics can execute JavaScript in the browser of any Prometheus user who views the metric in the heatmap chart UI. This vulnerability is fixed in 3.5.3 and 3.11.3.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-44903**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|github.com/prometheus/prometheus|0.311.3|[CVE-2026-44903](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-44903)|\n\nPrometheus is an open-source monitoring system and time series database. From 2.49.0 to before 3.5.3 and 3.11.3, in the Prometheus server's legacy web UI (enabled via the command-line flag --enable-feature=old-ui), the histogram heatmap chart view does not escape le label values when inserting them into the HTML for use as axis tick mark labels. An attacker who can inject crafted metrics can execute JavaScript in the browser of any Prometheus user who views the metric in the heatmap chart UI. This vulnerability is fixed in 3.5.3 and 3.11.3."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 6.1,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N",
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 5.1,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:N/SC:L/SI:L/SA:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "6.1",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "MEDIUM"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "GO-2026-5932",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "The golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp package is unmaintained, unsafe by design, and has known security issues"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp package is unsafe by design, has numerous known security issues, is not maintained, and should not be used.\n\nIf you are required to interoperate with OpenPGP systems and need a maintained package, consider github.com/ProtonMail/go-crypto/openpgp which is a maintained fork that aims to be a drop-in replacement for this package."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability GO-2026-5932\nSeverity: UNKNOWN\nPackage: golang.org/x/crypto\nFixed Version: \nLink: [GO-2026-5932]()\nThe golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp package is unsafe by design, has numerous known security issues, is not maintained, and should not be used.\n\nIf you are required to interoperate with OpenPGP systems and need a maintained package, consider github.com/ProtonMail/go-crypto/openpgp which is a maintained fork that aims to be a drop-in replacement for this package.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability GO-2026-5932**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|UNKNOWN|golang.org/x/crypto||[GO-2026-5932]()|\n\nThe golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp package is unsafe by design, has numerous known security issues, is not maintained, and should not be used.\n\nIf you are required to interoperate with OpenPGP systems and need a maintained package, consider github.com/ProtonMail/go-crypto/openpgp which is a maintained fork that aims to be a drop-in replacement for this package."
              },
